- An IAM role named `eks-cluster-1`
- An assume role policy allowing `eks.amazonaws.com` to assume the role
- Attachment of the AWS-managed `AmazonEKSClusterPolicy`
- A new VPC with public and private subnets across two Availability Zones
- Internet Gateway and route tables for public subnet routing
- An EKS cluster using the provided cluster name and Kubernetes version variables
- EKS networking configured with both public and private subnet IDs

